1
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,520
There you are.

2
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:26,310
P.E.'s already started.

3
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:31,350
They threw my gym clothes in the garbage.

4
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:33,520
Did they?

5
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:36,190
You're right, I remember that now.

6
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:42,150
Everyone's having so much fun. I hate them.

7
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:45,100
I did, didn't I?

8
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,020
I hate people in cliques, too.

9
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:51,810
Because it made me feel like I was
getting excluded for no good reason.

10
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:54,150
I hate breaks, too.

11
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:59,310
Because it felt like everyone was
pointing out how isolated I was.

12
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:03,190
I hated teachers, too, because
they made us work in groups,

13
00:01:03,190 --> 00:01:05,310
and I'd get excluded.

14
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:07,770
I especially hated special events at school.

15
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:13,770
Thinking back on those days, I can't
remember a single thing I didn't hate.

16
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:19,020
Nobody needs me around, anyway.

17
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:22,440
Can I just die?

18
00:01:26,150 --> 00:01:29,150
You should probably hold off on dying.

19
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:34,480
Wait a little longer and you'll make
a friend. An annoying one, but still.

20
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:39,730
You'll also meet a tall guy who's
kind and a girl who's friendly,

21
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:43,730
and a kinda-cowardly student council
president and his little posse.

22
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:48,310
Lots of people will want to be friends with you.

23
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:50,020
Not only that,

24
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,560
but you'll meet someone
who cries for you, laughs for you,

25
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:57,350
gets sad for you, gets mad for you,
and scolds you when you need scolding.

26
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:04,440
She's waiting for you, I promise.

27
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:07,940
If that's true, then...

28
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:13,230
Then...

29
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:20,190
Huh? What was I just dreaming about?

30
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:24,770
I wanna see Hori- <i>san</i> .

31
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:48,770
Horimiya

32
00:03:57,020 --> 00:04:00,310
The boy I love is really weak.

33
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,900
Really, really weak.

34
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:11,810
He doesn't actually like yelling at people.

35
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:17,190
He'll laugh about being unathletic,

36
00:04:17,190 --> 00:04:20,020
when really, he wishes he wasn't.

37
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:23,810
Boys and girls alike all fawn over him,

38
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:26,310
which makes him happy,

39
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:30,730
but every now and then,
it makes him feel anxious.

40
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:35,830
The Truth Deception Reveals

41
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:37,810
There's so much he struggles with,
and I love him so much.

42
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:52,270
O-Oh, no! Sengoku- <i>kun</i> , get it, I'm scared!

43
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:56,520
His expression screams "I'm scared, too!"

44
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,150
But...

45
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:05,020
That really freaked him out. Good job.

46
00:05:10,150 --> 00:05:16,690
The boy I love is weak,
but he tries really hard.

47
00:05:16,690 --> 00:05:18,850
But you know,

48
00:05:18,850 --> 00:05:23,270
back when we met,
he was a totally different person.

49
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:29,270
Man, I have such a crush on Ayasaki.

50
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:31,690
Her face is so tiny and cute, you know?

51
00:05:31,690 --> 00:05:33,310
Yeah, totally!

52
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:37,810
She's so hard to approach, though.
Like, she thinks she's too good for us.

53
00:05:37,810 --> 00:05:41,270
Probably 'cause she knows all
the guys have the hots for her.

54
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:45,690
Out of all the girls,
Ayasaki and Kono really stick out.

55
00:05:45,690 --> 00:05:47,480
They're like Beauty and the Beast.

56
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:50,400
You think so? They're both pretty normal.

57
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:53,520
C'mon, dude, Ayasaki's super hot.

58
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,480
Not really. They both look normal.

59
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:13,810
What were you reading in class just now?

60
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:15,690
Some manga?

61
00:06:15,690 --> 00:06:16,560
Goethe.

62
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,850
Gerta? What's that?

63
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:20,770
Goethe. He's an author.

64
00:06:20,770 --> 00:06:24,480
Oh, that's not the name of the book. Is it good?

65
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:26,900
Do you like to read, too, Ayasaki- <i>san</i> ?

66
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:31,270
Not during class, but yeah, I like reading.

67
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:32,940
Like <i>Grimm's Fairy Tales</i> .

68
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,400
You mean like, <i>Snow White</i> ?

69
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,900
Yeah, like <i>Snow White</i> .

70
